{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t","id":1290560,"title":"Marukan or Marukan't","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-21T15:51:12-08:00","id":1290560,"title":"Marukan or Marukan't","content":"One of my players has made up a Marukani conquering horselord Dawn character and we're all inspired by Ghengis Khan and shit, and I grab the second edition Scavenger Lands book for some stuff on the Marukani and maaaaaan I forgot how bad that writeup is. Let's make the Marukani into cowboy yokels boy howdy yeehah. <br /> <br /> So anyway we ditched most of the cultural specifics and went in a more Mongol direction because why wouldn't you! Mongols are objectively cooler than cowboys. <br /> <br /> I don't even really know where I'm going with this, I just needed to vent a bit. Yay third edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:31:48-08:00","id":1290588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t#post1290560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So anyway we ditched most of the cultural specifics and went in a more Mongol direction</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean they don't have a backstory of a long history of friendly and cooperative contact with the nations of the River Province, especially Lookshy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">because why wouldn't you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally? I find Mongols a bit played out, and actually think a society consisting of culturally tied but otherwise independent communities of plain ranchers to be interesting, if only because I'm not entirely sure any such society has existed historically.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T17:28:06-08:00","id":1290607,"title":"","content":"Played out in Exalted or in general? Because cowboys are preeeeeeeeeeetty played out in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T19:39:41-08:00","id":1290634,"title":"","content":"Say what you will, but the very fact that the nation of not-samurai is in a very old alliance with the nation of rancher-gaucho nomads is extremely elegant. If one considers that the Spaghetti Western, the genre rife with strong individualist protagonists relying on themselves and their weapons, is an extension of Samurai films, even more so.<br /> <br /> As per the prospect of an entire society built up around ranching, wasn't that the case with the Huns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:51:50-08:00","id":1290743,"title":"","content":"In the game I'm playing, we replaced them with Native Americans with horses - though unfortunately we've seen almost nothing of them in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T21:18:02-08:00","id":1290994,"title":"","content":"Eh, as someone who was playing a Marukani character all the way back in the first edition, I'd say Second Edition had a pretty good take on them. The Marukani have NEVER been a culture of raiders or conquerors. Ghengis Khan is pretty far outside their cultural wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T21:24:02-08:00","id":1290997,"title":"","content":"Since you're already changing absolutely everything about them anyway why not just come up with a different name in a slightly different part of the east that'd recently ridden over to the Scavenger Lands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T22:19:35-08:00","id":1291010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t?p=1290607#post1290607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Played out in Exalted or in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>Played out as an Internet thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because cowboys are preeeeeeeeeeetty played out in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, in cinematic terms, I think we've moved past the point of the Old West being played out, and there has recently been some interesting postmodern stuff that alternately analyses and deconstructs attitudes around it, or uses it as the setting of more contemplative, bleak, or just plain weird narratives. The kind of thing where the so-called frontier spirit is not depicted as a theatre for the American can-do spirit, of manly men and sassy women taming the wilderness, but of an edge of the world to which people who can't cope with society flee, and in which isolation breeds madness.<br /> <br /> So I guess that, in the end, the Reavers were less of an analogy for Native Americans than they were the actual frontiers people.<br /> <br /> (The Reavers as actually written are still totally a problematic analogy for Native Americans as narratively employed in older Westerns)<br /> <br /> But that's all tangential to Exalted (except insofar as it might be inspirational to some stories in the less populous Directions, or just the rim of the world in general). The main thing is that the cowboy elements are really only cosmetic, and don't retain much of the cultural context, which I stated why I think it's distinct and interesting.<br /> <br /> Really, in a fantasy fiction context, I think that part of why Mongols feel played out is because they're so often the go-to reference for a society of pastoral nomads associated with horses. Horses being basically the only thing that the Marukani have in common with the Mongols, and why I don't find them a good fit for overlaying.<br /> <br /> At least insofar as Internet discussions go. That you're having fun with what you're doing in your game is the most important thing, practically speaking.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:39:37-08:00","id":1291026,"title":"","content":"Ughh I\u2019m burnt out on postmodern deconstruction...<br /> <br /> But Mongol Aesthetics can vary widely, especially if you view them. It only as religiously syncretic but also Culturally. You have the Yuan Dynasty vibe of Kublai Khan mixing Mongols with China, a more pure Mongol Vibe with Ghengis Khan or pre Ghengis Khan people\u2019s like the Tartars. And folks like the Mughals who have that whole Muslim Indian vibe (probably closer to how the Tri-Khan\u2019s aesthetics).<br /> <br /> But I think the Solution is Clear!<br /> <br /> ...Mongol Cowboys...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:11:00-08:00","id":1291034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gatts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t?p=1290743#post1290743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the game I'm playing, we replaced them with Native Americans with horses - though unfortunately we've seen almost nothing of them in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I like to think of them.<br /> <br /> Cowboys doesn't fit my idea of Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T07:49:12-08:00","id":1291128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t?p=1291034#post1291034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cowboys doesn't fit my idea of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the aesthetic for individual characters, but when you're presenting an entire nation or culture drawing from such an well known and influential source leads people to half-read the text then fill in the blanks with what they're familiar with.<br /> <br /> The Marukani soldiers in Compass Scavenger Lands look nothing like cowboys, but who honestly remembers that when everything about them otherwise screams cowboy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T08:10:47-08:00","id":1291135,"title":"","content":"The thing I remember most about the Marukani is that someone slipped a little tidbit into the 2e book about how one tribe practices, shall we say, endogamy to an extremely unpleasant degree. Which is all nasty and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T08:38:07-08:00","id":1291142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t?p=1291128#post1291128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the aesthetic for individual characters, but when you're presenting an entire nation or culture drawing from such an well known and influential source leads people to half-read the text then fill in the blanks with what they're familiar with.<br /> <br /> The Marukani soldiers in Compass Scavenger Lands look nothing like cowboys, but who honestly remembers that when everything about them otherwise screams cowboy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, re-reading the description, there's bits where it's very cowboy (&quot;they're masters of the whip and firewand, and never go anywhere without their cowhide hats&quot;; &quot;each town has a general store full of knick-knacks&quot;).<br /> <br /> And then there's other bits where it's not all. Their towns have amphitheatres, their soldiers fight with lances or bows and wear Lookshy-made (so Japanese-looking) armour. Their elite soldiers are heavily-armoured cataphractoi with hammers. Their social organisation is all about clans.<br /> And the Marukani girl in Castebook: Eclipse doesn't look like a cowgirl at all.<br /> <br /> Also, cattle are mentioned 3 times... but it also mentions sheep, pigs and wheat.<br /> <br /> I think the idea was, you know, not to make a sphaghetti culture of spaghetti Cowboys/Mongols/Samurai, but to take bits from all over the place and make a unique culture (which is a good idea).<br /> But, as you say, as cowboys are a big influence on them, people take that and assume that's the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Also, tbh, they don't have a lot of other interesting features to get past that, IMO (but maybe I'm biased; I consider Compass: Scavenger Lands the worst Compass of Terrestrial Directions).<br /> <br /> I guess the same way as other places get labelled &quot;Japan-land&quot; or &quot;Viking land&quot;.<br /> <br /> (At least Medo was described by Holden as &quot;Mongol Transylvania&quot; so that's not just one thing.)<br /> <br /> I don't know about Scavenger Sons (I don't own a copy), but Outcastes just calls them &quot;horselords&quot; and talks about their alliance, and how they provide horses to Lookshy.<br /> This mostly makes me think of the Rohirrim, tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-23-2019, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:33:50-08:00","id":1291154,"title":"","content":"Yeah, what the fuck is the firewand even doing in Marukan? It just adds to that wild west imagery it can't really deliver on due to being in the wrong part of the world and flame weapons are short-ranged flamethrowers that don't really do 19th century firearms justice.<br /> <br /> This is before we get into questions of where the firedust was supposed to come from. Lookshy I guess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-23-2019, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:40:02-08:00","id":1291159,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I can't really see Lookshy having enough firedust to sell. They have to buy it at exorbitant cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:43:13-08:00","id":1291160,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What makes a cowboy? Is it the cosmetic elements (which were all things creates by practical considerations for the environment they were operating in, rather than making a fashion statement)? Is it the cultural context, of being on the frontier of an expanding national interest, and furnishing the growing meat market that accompanies general economic prosperity? Or something in the attitude?</span></span></span></div><br /> Mind, I take Lioness' point. I can't in good faith even call readings that stop or overlook elements because of that first impression a reading in bad faith, if I'm willing to acknowledge or consider elsewhere in which readings of a text can be shaped by emphasis or particular imagery and that some of the onus for ensuring something is read in a desired manner falls on the writer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t?p=1291142#post1291142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider Compass: Scavenger Lands the worst Compass of Terrestrial Directions).</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree (would phrase it as &quot;weakest&quot; over &quot;worst&quot;), with the exception of the antagonists chapter. I think Scavenger Lands got the best spirit write-ups before Compass: North, benefiting as it did from needing to write those folks before the general spirit Charms were put together. Even the Compass: North ones are constrained by that, managing to make up for it through sheer personality. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about Scavenger Sons (I don't own a copy), but Outcastes just calls them &quot;horselords&quot; and talks about their alliance, and how they provide horses to Lookshy.<br /> This mostly makes me think of the Rohirrim, tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slander! The Eorlingas will not give up their horses for love nor money.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:48:09-08:00","id":1291161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t?p=1291154#post1291154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">flame weapons are short-ranged flamethrowers that don't really do 18th century firearms justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume you mean 19th century?<br /> <br /> When I hear about flame weapons and cavalry, I generally assume that their combat tactic is to caracole. I'm not saying that necessarily means it makes sense for the Marukan in particular to have them, just a response to general criticisms of them being associated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:58:31-08:00","id":1291166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290560-marukan-or-marukan-t?p=1291161#post1291161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume you mean 19th century?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, went to type 1800s then thought century would look better and forgot to change the actual number.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I hear about flame weapons and cavalry, I generally assume that their combat tactic is to caracole. I'm not saying that necessarily means it makes sense for the Marukan in particular to have them, just a response to general criticisms of them being associated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its less a realism concern with cavalry and more that someone looking for that kind of cinematic action is going to be badly disapointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-23-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T06:47:12-08:00","id":1291517,"title":"","content":"Marukan having firewands was of course not a thing in Scavenger Sons. The other major difference in presentation was that Scavenger Sons gave stats for the various breeds of horses that were absent from 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T06:53:58-08:00","id":1291519,"title":"","content":"I think having them just use bows on horseback, even if they live on ranches and are very individualist, gives them a very different feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T21:19:59-08:00","id":1291715,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, &amp; I'd like to encourage you with the story of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khutulun\" target=\"_blank\">Khutulun</a>, the Mongol Princess who refused to marry any man who couldn't beat her at wrestling, and demanded that her suitors put up a bunch of horses if they wanted to try. Apparently she ended up with 10,000 horses before she finally relented &amp; married a man for political reasons without wrestling him first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"